    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d409">

                <pb facs="1823" n="1672" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v07-09mSupp/pg1672"/>

                <head>409. Memorandum from Komer to Coffin, May 2<anchor n="1" xml:id="d409-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1962-05-02">May 2, 1962</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d409-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d409-1"/>
                <p>Frank, forgive this rather long and rambling discourse, but as you know my
                    heart’s in the right place. I see your report on MAP/AID coordination as the
                    charter you need to bring MAP under control, and am anxious to give all the help
                    I can.</p>
                <closer><signed>R.W. Komer</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d409-a1.xml" xpointer="d409-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d409-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d409-f1-content">
                <p>AID draft on improving coordination of military and economic aid programs.
                    Secret. 4 pp. Kennedy Library, National Security Files, Kaysen Series, Foreign
                    Aid, General, 5/62–11/63, Box 373.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
